This project builds on third-party work:

- agens-engine (https://github.com/BlockWayz/agens-engine), MIT License, by BlockWayz.
  This is the numerics reference for the port; the parity tooling uses its file formats. The file
  volundr-mlx/bench/long_prompt.txt contains an excerpt of its kernels/m1/m1_model.cu.

- Agens Volundr release code (https://huggingface.co/Blockway/Agens-Volundr-32B-v1-INT4),
  Apache License 2.0, by Blockway.
  volundr-mlx/tests/reference.py ports modeling_volundr.py, bcsa.py and volundr_extras.py to NumPy, and the
  model in volundr-mlx/volundr.py follows their math.

- MLX and mlx-lm (https://github.com/ml-explore), MIT License, Copyright Apple Inc.
  volundr-mlx/kernels.py extends mlx-lm's gated-delta Metal kernel, and adapts MLX's neural-accelerator
  attention. The MLX headers it uses are read from the installed MLX package at run time; they are not
  included here.

Not included:

- Model weights. They are subject to the licenses in their Hugging Face repositories, including the Qwen3.8
  license that ships there.

- The speculative-decoding prompt suite (volundr-mlx/spec/suite.json). volundr-mlx/spec/make_suite.py builds it
  locally from SPEED-Bench, MMLU, ARC-Challenge, BoolQ and SWE-smith, whose own licenses apply.
